tion"],"visibility":"public","forks":4446,"open_issues":734,"watchers":27145,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Vagrant is reporting that I have an outdated box. When I try to update it says that I am running the latest version. There is a new version but it is for a different provider. \r\n\r\nBox in question:\r\nhttps://app.vagrantup.com/bento/boxes/centos-7\r\n\r\nProvider I am using:\r\nvirtualbox\r\n\r\n### Vagrant version\r\nVagrant 2.2.6\r\n\r\n### Host operating system\r\nMacOS 10.14.6 Mojave\r\n\r\n### Guest operating system\r\nCentos-7 via virtualbox\r\n\r\n### Debug output\r\nhttps://gist.github.com/iammoen/f2dbd5091c4e81266f5abbeb76d6f1e9\r\nTwo files are in the gist, one for the outdated command, one for the update command.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n```\r\n$ vagrant box outdated --global\r\n* 'bento/centos-7' for 'virtualbox' (v201910.20.1) is up to date\r\n``` \r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n```\r\n$ vagrant box outdated --global\r\n* 'bento/centos-7' for 'virtualbox' is outdated! Current: 201910.20.1. Latest: 201910.21.0\r\n``` \r\nThen if you try to update the box via `vagrant box update bento/centos-7` the response is\r\n```\r\nChecking for updates to 'bento/centos-7'\r\nLatest installed version: 201910.20.1\r\nVersion constraints: > 201910.20.1\r\nProvider: virtualbox\r\nBox 'bento/centos-7' (v201910.20.1) is running the latest version.\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n1. `vagrant box add bento/centos-7`\r\n2. `vagrant box outdated --global`\r\n3. `vagrant box update --box bento/centos-7`\r\n4. `vagrant box outdated --global`\r\n\r\n### References\r\nAre there any other GitHub issues (open or closed) that should be linked here?\r\nThis might be relevant? https://github.com/hashicorp/vagrant/issues/9044","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hashicorp/vagrant/issues/11163/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused"